      },
      "message": "feat(pick): circle and arc centres as opt-in feature points\n\nA picker that takes points can now opt in to the centre of a round\nfeature edge (PickKinds::centres). The centre is stored as the round\nrun it comes from and read back through #759's circle_of_run. It is\noffered only while its edge is in sight; with Pick-through on it is\noffered even when the edge is hidden. The three-points draft and an\naxis by two points opt in. No other picker does. Those point slots, in\nthe GUI and over MCP (lay_part_on_points, set_part_axes), read a\ncircular edge chain as its centre. A straight or non-circular edge is\nrefused by name.\n\nRefs #692\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAAAJyAPrC37zBzbbX",
